WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.230
600 meters to go!

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:05.740
I've kept myself under wraps for a long time!

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.030
Despite my behavior,
 I have a lot of restraint!

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:09.430
<i>Pressure...</i>

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.060
<i>And not as another participant.</i>

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.990
<i>Pressure as a human. He's strong.</i>

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:18.100
Interesting. It seems 
you're a worthy opponent.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.000
I'll win. And Hakone Academy will 
achieve its first true victory!

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.270
Muscles don't lie!

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.620
Let's race, Kishigami-kun!

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.130
Let's see who crosses the sprint line first!

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:29.890
Are you ready?

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.630
Here we go, Andy, Frank. It's our final...

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.710
<i>Our final job!</i>

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:39.220
500 meters remain to the Inter-High's 
second day's sprint line!

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.220
<i>We'll take the sprint!</i>

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.350
Abs, abs, abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.700
Buaaa!

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.930
I told you, I can read your movements.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:49.770
I just told you.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.900
#116's reactions are so fast!

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.420
Muscles are honest. Fakes don't work.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.950
You order them to move, 
and they enter the motion.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.910
They begin moving hundredths of 
seconds before they enter the motion.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.570
Especially yours, Izumida-san.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:07.130
Your muscles are particularly honest.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.540
And I won't miss a thing.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:14.970
I will win because I know everything 
you'll do before the finish line!

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.390
<i>He's in front?</i>

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.770
Kyoto Fushimi's accelerating now?

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.350
Hakone Academy got a late start!

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:29.420
<i>He took advantage of a moment's opening!</i>

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.160
<i>I can't believe he's jumping ahead now!</i>

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.530
Kyoto Fushimi's staying ahead!

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.780
Abs, abs, abs!

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.430
There's 200 meters left!

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:42.060
After the corner, there's only 
80 meters to the sprint line!

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.450
Is he going to do it?

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.840
<i>I don't care about their cheers.</i>

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.810
<i>I want to touch muscles. That's all.</i>

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:53.460
<i>There's nothing blocking me anymore!</i>

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.340
<b>Day Two</b>

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.850
The top racers competing 
for the sprint are coming!

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.680
It's Kyoto Fushimi and Hakone Academy!

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:24.490
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.490
Go, Kyoto Fushimi!

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:48.010
<i>LINE.15  The Sprint Line of Delight</i>

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.490
Hakone Academy!

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:50.500
<i>One hundred meters to the sprint line!</i>

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:54.380
<i>The line is just on the other 
side of this left turn!</i>

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.380
<i>There's nothing blocking me anymore!</i>

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:03.390
<i>He's ahead of me.</i>

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.570
<i>But just barely.</i>

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.840
<i>There's 100 meters left.</i>

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.180
<i>I'll wait to brake until the last second...</i>

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:16.400
<i>And force my body</i>

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.530
<i>into the inside of the last corner!</i>

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:23.210
<i>I did it.</i>

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:25.200
<i>There's only 80 meters to the finish line.</i>

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.990
<i>It's an all-out sprint!</i>

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:30.790
What?

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.950
There's something on the course!

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:37.210
<i>A plastic bottle?</i>

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:41.780
<i>It's not uncommon for debris 
to be on the course.</i>

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.130
<i>But this timing...</i>

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.100
<i>Kishighami's ahead of me and moving fast.</i>

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.430
<i>Should I charge ahead and risk falling</i>

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:57.400
<i>or brake to avoid danger?</i>

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:01.580
<i>I don't have much time or distance left.</i>

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.990
<i>I can see the line.</i>

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:10.570
<i>If I brake at this speed, I'll lose 
seconds and the chance to win.</i>

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:19.420
<i>Andy and Frank are ordering me to avoid it. 
"It's too dangerous. Squeeze the brakes."</i>

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.010
<i>They're absolutely right.</i>

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.760
<i>There's no reason to deliberately take risks</i>

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:27.370
<i>when you're not at the finish line!</i>

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:33.180
<i>I'll never win anything unless I take 
risks and desperately charge ahead.</i>

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.810
<i>Isn't that what I learned?</i>

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:44.170
Andy, Frank... I'm sorry.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.990
Please be quiet!

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:56.000
<i>What's important is identifying your goal,</i>

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:59.580
<i>and how much of a risk you can take.</i>

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:04.800
<i>So I must charge straight 
ahead without hesitation!</i>

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:07.750
<i>Toward my goal!</i>

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:11.510
Abs, abs, abs, abs, buaaa!

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:15.280
Straight ahead? No way!

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.770
Does he not see it?

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.190
His rear tire slipped!

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.410
He's falling!

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.330
<i>Control!</i>

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:32.620
<i>Shift your weight and maintain your posture</i>

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.120
<i>without letting up on the pedals.</i>

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.870
<i>Hold your posture!</i>

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:40.750
<i>Hold it!</i>

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:45.550
How unlucky.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:47.810
Excuse me while I go on ahead.

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:50.860
<i>Hold it!</i>

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:58.370
<i>My tire's grip is back.</i>

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.350
<i>From now on, it's all out!</i>

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.360
Abs, abs, abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.870
He just barely restored his posture!

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:07.070
He's accelerating!

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:11.030
<i>And don't take your eyes off your goal.</i>

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.450
Abs, abs, abs, abs, abs, abs!

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:14.450
<i>"Unlucky."</i>

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:17.070
<i>Let me tell you, Kishigami...</i>

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:22.420
<i>You can't know that for sure 
until the line's been crossed.</i>

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:27.030
<i>"Unlucky" can be changed to "lucky."</i>

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:32.010
<i>And that's something only 
you can do for yourself!</i>

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.620
Hakone Academy's closing!

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:39.830
Was he resting his legs while 
pedaling when he slipped?

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:48.110
Idiot.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.930
Quit your crying, Izumida.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:55.470
But Hakone Academy placed second!

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.700
I... I...

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:01.660
Crying about second place is our job.

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:04.120
What?

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:09.340
If you place second again next year, 
you can cry your eyes out then.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:11.880
You've still got a job to do.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:16.720
Tedious stuff like analyzing and 
deciding what needs to be strengthened.

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:21.180
Your results aren't out yet.

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:24.350
So...

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.860
Achieve something next year.

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:31.470
Yes, sir!

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.400
I will!

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:35.990
Abuaaa!

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:39.990
50 meters left! They're neck and neck!

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:43.160
<i>What is he doing here?</i>

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:46.880
<i>No, that doesn't matter right now.</i>

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:49.210
<i>I just need to keep racing toward the line,</i>

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:52.460
<i>so I can touch those good muscles!</i>

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:55.700
Izumida caught up!

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.680
Go, Kishigami!

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:00.310
They're both going all out!

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:02.410
40 meters...

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:03.900
...remaining!

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:11.070
<i>Tremble, my muscles!</i>

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:14.490
<i>They're screaming.</i>

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:18.780
<i>All the muscles in my body.</i>

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:25.330
<i>My abused muscle fibers are tearing audibly.</i>

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:31.550
<i>And my burdened muscle fibers 
will heal overnight when I rest.</i>

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:36.940
<i>They will become stronger, thicker, 
and more flexible as they heal.</i>

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:40.670
<i>Those are the basics of strength training.</i>

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:46.850
<i>I've always felt the sprint 
before the finish line...</i>

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.900
<i>Going all out. That tension.</i>

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:54.780
<i>For me, that is the ultimate 
strength training!</i>

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:57.700
Abs!

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:02.670
<i>Andy, Frank. And you, Fabian.</i>

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:06.160
<i>I'm sorry for ignoring your warning earlier.</i>

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.470
<i>Thank you for listening to me.</i>

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:11.460
<i>It's all right now.</i>

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:14.220
<i>Come on out. Come on.</i>

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.700
<i>And rampage to your heart's content!</i>

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:25.970
<i>For our Hakone Academy's victory!</i>

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:37.690
<i>Compress my heart, pump blood through 
my body, take oxygen into my chest,</i>

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:42.030
<i>and push me beyond light speed!</i>

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:50.240
<i>Beyond!</i>

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.290
Abuaaa!

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:58.050
Hakone Academy pulled slightly ahead!

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.450
<i>Ahead?</i>

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:02.220
<i>But he just slipped back there!</i>

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:07.560
<i>Is the acceleration of 
Hakone Academy's #4 this...</i>

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:12.550
<i>This? This?</i>

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.740
<i>Huh? I can see it...</i>

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:20.930
<i>A field of flowers!</i>

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:24.070
<i>I see it!</i>

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.710
A field of muscles!

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:38.340
Kyoto Fushimi accelerated again!

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:44.140
Most guys lose hope and decelerate when 
they're passed before the finish line,

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:45.680
but he's still pedaling!

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:48.680
What incredible mental strength!

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:51.940
A field!

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:55.310
Abuaaa!

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.950
Abs!

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:05.620
<i>Yuki...</i>

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:07.700
<i>Takuto...</i>

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:09.420
<i>Doubashi...</i>

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:11.350
<i>Yuto...</i>

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:13.830
<i>Manami...</i>

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:22.590
<i>The winner of the second day's sprint is...</i>

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:27.420
<i>Sorry to keep you waiting.</i>

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:33.940
<i>Hakone Academy #14, third-year, captain,</i>

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:37.490
<i>Izumida Touichirou!</i>

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:41.940
Abua! Abua! Abua!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:49.660
<i>Now the champions truly have 
reclaimed their throne!</i>

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:55.580
Izumida-san!

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:56.490
Captain!

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:58.210
You did it, Izumida-san!

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:02.710
Thanks, guys.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:05.800
Izumida-san, over here!

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:17.850
Shin... Shinkai-san...

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:22.360
I came to watch, Izumida.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.830
That was an awesome sprint.

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.250
<i>Shinkai-san...</i>

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:40.790
<i>Shinkai-san.</i>

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:45.020
<i>It was a heavy and difficult year.</i>

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.890
<i>"A sprinter can't be the captain."</i>

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.770
<i>"Last year's loss."</i>

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:58.230
<i>There were times I nearly couldn't 
withstand those pressures.</i>

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:05.140
<i>But now I feel like some 
of it's been wiped away.</i>

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.820
<i>I carried the strong Hakone 
Academy team on my back,</i>

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:16.410
<i>created a new team with my teammates,
 and carved a new path.</i>

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:20.420
<i>Shinkai-san...</i>

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:24.150
<i>Shinkai-san, am I...</i>

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.890
<i>on the right path?</i>

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.610
<i>Izumida...</i>

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:35.770
<i>The captain's position and tag #4...</i>

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:39.700
<i>I'm glad we entrusted both of those to you.</i>

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:43.690
<i>You're the pride of Hakone Academy.</i>

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.830
<i>You're the fastest man!</i>

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:48.750
Abs!

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:50.700
Hakone Academy is amazing!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.830
I got chills!

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:55.870
<i>Shinkai-san,</i>

00:14:58.170 --> 00:14:59.710
<i>thank you so—</i>

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:08.810
<i>That's Shinkai-san's Kapow Pose.</i>

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:11.140
<i>It means he'll definitely 
take down his target.</i>

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:14.510
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:19.420
<i>Now it's a kapow of appreciation.</i>

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:25.170
Thank you!

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:28.910
He's gone.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.690
It was only for a moment.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:33.450
If this were the finish line, 
we could've talked longer.

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:36.500
A moment...

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:42.970
Some things can only be conveyed in a moment.

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:57.140
I wanted to touch them!

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:00.100
<i>Kishigami Komari...</i>

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.440
I was supposed to be able to touch them.

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:07.940
I pulled ahead 300 meters before the line.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:12.740
You closed the gap during the turn, 
but then you slipped on some debris.

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:15.920
I thought I had won.

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:20.120
After all, from your muscle mass
 and movements, I expected

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:24.250
that you wouldn't catch me
 by the end of the sprint!

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:26.500
But you did.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:30.210
In other words, it was that moment.

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:33.430
In that moment, your muscles...

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:38.470
They became larger, stronger...

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:45.100
And far more swollen than I had imagined!

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:47.970
More virile!

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:50.190
Fiercer!

00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:55.510
Your muscles exceeded my expectations.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:00.690
They are the highest-quality muscles.

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:04.620
How did you forge them?

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:07.610
I thought I knew.

00:17:08.990 --> 00:17:16.630
But your muscles exceeded my imagination.

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:22.390
Do you want to touch my muscles?

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:31.730
I don't mind. After all, the race is over.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:54.330
No, thank you.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:18:00.470
I made a rule that I would only touch 
them if I crossed the line first.

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:03.530
<i>A rule?</i>

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:09.370
<i>This man has his own aesthetic, too.</i>

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:13.060
What a sportsman.

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:17.310
Though you're my opponent, 
I admire your spirit.

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:21.950
No, I was just raised that way.

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:27.650
I really wanted to touch them.

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:37.330
<i>This guy is still a first-year.</i>

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:39.900
<i>Whatever his motivation,</i>

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:46.310
<i>as long as he keeps riding, he may 
eventually pose a threat to Hakone Academy.</i>

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:50.730
<i>No, I should be focusing 
on this race right now.</i>

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:55.150
<i>The sprint is over.</i>

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:59.420
<i>The course will be flat for 
a while, but after that,</i>

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:02.730
<i>we'll enter the mountain stage.</i>

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:06.620
<i>The climbers will make their move.</i>

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:09.960
<b>Day Two</b>

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:09.960
Thanks for coming.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:14.040
Really, thank you so much for 
coming to watch the race.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:16.930
There's no need to be so considerate of me.

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:20.680
Is everyone who graduated doing well?

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:25.180
Why don't you ask them yourself?

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.210
Fu...

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:35.220
Fukutomi-san!

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:40.450
I felt more nervous watching him.

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:42.950
I felt more relaxed when I was riding.

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:47.540
Did you not want him to see you, Juichi?

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:52.290
No. Just watching his sprint was enough.

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:57.970
He managed to wipe away 
the guilt he was carrying.

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:00.420
Izumida did well.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:04.790
He would've been happy to hear that from you.

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:09.930
Hakone Academy's captain isn't 
someone who should be praised.

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:12.730
You're strict.

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:16.830
Come to think of it, I heard
 he was coming today.

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:18.610
Is he late?

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:21.110
No. I got a call this morning.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:25.230
He's watching from somewhere else today.

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:35.750
<b>Day Two
Mountain Line</b>

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:39.590
It's still going to be another 
hour before any riders get here.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:41.670
No, more than that.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:46.300
<b>Day Two
Mountain Line</b>

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:45.250
I wonder who will win the 
second day's mountain result.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:57.270
Not who, but which.

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:02.030
It will be decided.

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:06.200
After all, this is the only stage

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:11.090
where they can race without any distractions.

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:14.910
For the King of the Mountain...

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:20.470
To inherit the title of Mountain God.

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:27.020
And I, Toudou Jinpachi, will watch over 
the entirety of their mountain race.

00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:08.190
<i>Shinkai-san, look at how much I've 
grown while spending time with you!</i>

00:23:10.970 --> 00:23:12.030
Shinkai-san!

00:23:14.130 --> 00:23:15.740
Would you like some of this, too?

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:19.160
Shinkai-san!

00:23:20.570 --> 00:23:21.620
This is for you!

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:25.500
It's a special tropical melon drink!

00:23:25.990 --> 00:23:27.090
Shinkai-san!

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:29.190
Shinkai-san!

00:23:29.190 --> 00:23:30.380
Shinkai-san!

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:31.880
<i>Kapow.</i>

00:23:33.230 --> 00:23:35.500
<i>A kapow of appreciation!</i>

00:23:36.490 --> 00:23:39.890
<i>NEXT LINE  Sohoku Falls Behind</i>

